rom_browser: allow an OS-managed deliberate whole-library scan

Rasteratops' explicit preparation scans must retain more than100 games in
one run (D-RA-014, #361). Add an opt-in budgeted=False argument to the
single-ROM/drain entrypoints. Existing upstream callers keep the100-game
window and batch bound. Deliberate calls retain the queue locks, pacing,
429 stop and persisted pause; each cached game is still charged. They do
not treat queued success as readiness: the integrating helper checks queued.

The original patch004 raised a removed total-library cap. This replacement
preserves that workflow through current upstream's queue API instead.

